libnfc - the NFC protocol stacks of the Flipper, as plain C (spec Phase 14)
===========================================================================

Issue #387, spec Phase 14 (R14.*, AC14.1, AC14.2), D.3, D.4.  The stock
`nfc` app's protocol layer, over one abstract transceiver, so it is written
and host-tested now and meets the ST25R3916 driver (Phase 13, lane:local)
later at one small interface.  Stock is the behaviour reference; code is
reused from stock `lib/nfc` and Unleashed `lib/nfc/protocols` (both GPL-3.0,
D.3/D.4).

The one interface (this is the whole contract with the driver)
---------------------------------------------------------------
  nfc_xfer.h        the transceiver: nfc_xfer_t.transceive(buf, bits,
                    flags) plus field/poll/delay hooks.  Three things fill
                    it in: the ST25R3916 driver (/dev/nfc, <minix/nfc.h>),
                    a host card model (flipper/tests/nfc), a QEMU mock.
  <minix/nfc.h>     the /dev/nfc ioctls the driver will give (kernel
                    <= +200 B, Phase 13).  See
                    docs/devguide/nfc-driver-interface.md.

Done so far
----------
  crypto1.c/.h      MIFARE Classic Crypto-1 cipher and the tag PRNG.
                    D.3: ciphers are ported in full; no keys are shipped.
                    Public algorithm (Crapto1, GPL-2.0-or-later -> GPL-3.0),
                    reimplemented from the published polynomials.
  mf_classic.c/.h   MIFARE Classic data model, reader-side three-pass
                    authentication, block read, SAK -> type.
  mf_dict.c/.h      the key dictionary read a line at a time (never whole).
  mf_attack.c/.h    the dictionary attack as a streaming loop (AC14.2).
  nfc_file.c/.h     the stock `.nfc` file reader/writer (AC14.1).
  iso14443_3a.c/.h  the NFC-A poller: REQA, the anticollision cascade
                    (4/7/10-byte UIDs) and SELECT.
  mf_ultralight.c/.h  MIFARE Ultralight / NTAG: GET_VERSION -> subtype,
                    page READ.
  nfc_poller.c/.h   the top of the reader: poll -> identify by SAK ->
                    read (MIFARE Classic with the found keys, Ultralight
                    by page) into the nfc_device the file writer saves.

All of the above is host-tested in flipper/tests/nfc (software 3A,
MIFARE Classic 1K and NTAG215 card models) under ASan/UBSan.

The vendored Unleashed stacks (src/lib/nfc, unchanged) on nfc_xfer (#404):
  nfc_shim.c/.h     furi, FuriString and the `Nfc` API over nfc_xfer; the
                    poller loop runs in the caller (step cap, no threads).
  nfc_shim_mfc.c    thread flags without threads, and failing storage/
                    stream/key-dictionary stubs for the MIFARE Classic
                    poller's attack modes and nfc_device.c's file half.
  nfc_shim_time.c   stock's datetime/locale (24 h, D.M.Y) and RTC calls.
  nfc_poller_defs_shim.c, nfc_device_defs_shim.c
                    the poller and device tables of the protocols built:
                    3A, 3B, 4A, 4B, DESFire, 15693, SLIX, MIFARE Classic
                    (with stock's mf_classic_poller_sync).
  nfc_supported_cards.c/.h, nfc_supported_cards_list.h
                    the supported_cards parsers linked in (no plugin
                    loader): verify -> read with the parser's keys ->
                    parse to text.  25 of the 41 build today.
  shim/             the headers the vendored files include.
Tested in flipper/tests/nfc/prototest.c and cardtest.c (software 4A, 4B,
DESFire, SLIX2 and MIFARE Classic 1K/4K models).

Memory rules (spec Phase 14)
----------------------------
No big buffer stays resident: every protocol context is allocated per use
and freed; the libraries cost flash only (XIP).  The dictionary is streamed
from /home/flipper/nfc/assets a line at a time, never loaded whole.

Still to port (needs the Unleashed lib/nfc tree copied byte for byte the
way src/lib/subghz and src/lib/lfrfid were; that tree is not in this
runner, so these are not reimplemented from memory):
  - the parsers that are not in the table yet: those that read ID or
    station lists from files (plantain, sevppk_tk, sk_tk, szppk_so,
    skylanders: D.3, the user's own files on the SD card), those on
    protocols not built here (Ultralight/NTAG, FeliCa, ST25TB, EMV),
    disney_infinity (SHA-1) and banapass (case labels on const objects,
    which GCC rejects);
  - the full `mfkey` nonce recovery (lfsr_recovery32/64, nested): the
    Crapto1 state-recovery, to be copied verbatim, not rewritten.
Lane:local (the driver): the ST25R3916 /dev/nfc back end for nfc_xfer,
card emulation (NFCIOCLISTEN), the field detector, the on-device `nfc`
GUI app and `mfkey` nonce collection, and AC14.3 field tests.
